#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:240
msgid ""
"Because <application>Gnumeric</application> automatically guesses the data "
"type of a number being entered into a cell, this process may have to be "
"over-ridden for certain types of data. For example, postal codes in the "
"United States consist of a sequence of numbers which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> interprets as an integer. However, U.S. "
"postal codes can start with a leading zero which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> discards by default. In order to "
"override the default format, the number format of the cell must be specified"
" before the entry of the data. This is explained in <xref linkend=\"number-"
"formatting-overview\"/>, below."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom <application>Gnumeric</application> automatiskt gissar datatypen "
"för ett tal som matas in kan du behöva åsidosätta den för vissa slags data. "
"Postnummer i USA består till exempel av siffror som "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> tolkar som heltal. Amerikanska "
"postnummer kan dock börja med noll, som <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"tar bort som standard. Om du vill behålla nollan måste du ange cellens "
"talformat innan du matar in värdet. Detta beskrivs nedan i <xref "
"linkend=\"number-formatting-overview\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:260
msgid ""
"Cells can contain boolean data elements. These elements arise from Boolean "
"logic which is a branch of mathematics. These elements are useful for "
"manipulation of formulas."
msgstr ""
"Celler kan innehålla booleska dataelement. De bygger på boolesk logik, en "
"gren av matematiken, och används vid hantering av formler."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:266
msgid ""
"Boolean values can be either \"TRUE\" or \"FALSE\". If these strings are "
"entered into a cell, <application>Gnumeric</application> will recognize "
"these as boolean values. These values can then be used in formulas. Certain "
"formulas will also return boolean values."
msgstr ""
"Booleska värden kan vara ”TRUE” eller ”FALSE”. Om du skriver in någon av "
"dessa strängar i en cell känner <application>Gnumeric</application> igen den"
" som ett booleskt värde. Värdena kan sedan användas i formler, och vissa "
"formler returnerar också booleska värden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:299
msgid ""
"Formulas are the key to making a powerful spreadsheet. A formula instructs "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> to perform calculations and display the "
"results. These calculations are defined as a formula data elements. The "
"power of these formulas arises because these formulas can include the "
"contents of other cells and the results of the formulas are updated "
"automatically when the contents of any cell included in the formula change. "
"The contents of other cells are included using \"cell references\" which are"
" explained below."
msgstr ""
"Formler gör kalkylblad kraftfulla. En formel instruerar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> att utföra en beräkning och visa "
"resultatet. Formler kan använda innehållet i andra celler, och resultatet "
"uppdateras automatiskt när innehållet i någon av dessa celler ändras. Du "
"hänvisar till andra celler med cellreferenser, som beskrivs nedan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:311
msgid ""
"Any formula entered into a cell must follow a specific syntax so that "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> can interpret the formula correctly. "
"This syntax closely follows mathematical notation but also includes "
"spreadsheet formulas, object names and cell references."
msgstr ""
"Formler som matas in i en cell måste följa en viss syntax för att "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> ska kunna tolka dem rätt. Syntaxen "
"följer i stort matematisk notation men omfattar också kalkylbladsformler, "
"objektnamn och cellreferenser."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:322
msgid ""
"Formulas are distinguished from regular data by starting with an equals sign"
" (=) as the first character. Everything following this equals sign is "
"evaluated as a formula."
msgstr ""
"Formler skiljs från vanliga data genom att börja med ett likhetstecken (=). "
"Allt som följer efter tecknet tolkas som en formel."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:331
msgid ""
"To accommodate those more familiar with Lotus spreadsheets, Gnumeric "
"recognizes the commercial at symbol (@) as the beginning of a formula and "
"substitutes an equals sign. The plus and minus characters (+ and -) may also"
" start formulas that involve calculation, but when used in front of a single"
" number only indicate the sign of the number."
msgstr ""
"För att underlätta för användare som är vana vid Lotus-kalkylblad känner "
"Gnumeric igen snabel-a (@) som början på en formel och byter ut det mot ett "
"likhetstecken. Plus- och minustecknen (+ och -) kan också inleda beräknande "
"formler, men framför ett ensamt tal anger de bara talets tecken."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:341
msgid ""
"The simplest formulas just use the standard math operator and symbols. "
"Addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division are represented by +, -,"
" *, and /, just as you would expect. +,- can be placed in front of numbers "
"to indicate sign, as well. <_:example-1/>"
msgstr ""
"De enklaste formlerna använder vanliga matematiska operatorer och symboler. "
"Addition, subtraktion, multiplikation och division skrivs med +, -, * "
"respektive /. Plus- och minustecken kan också stå framför tal för att ange "
"deras tecken. <_:example-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:365
msgid ""
"Formulas can result in error values in several instances. If a formula is "
"entered incorrectly, <application>Gnumeric</application> will display a "
"warning and allow either the formula to be corrected or will save the "
"formula as text for editing later. If a syntactically correct formula "
"results in a nonsensical calculation (for instance, a division by zero), "
"then an error value will be displayed indicating the error."
msgstr ""
"Formler kan ge felvärden av flera orsaker. Om en formel är felaktigt inmatad"
" visar <application>Gnumeric</application> en varning och låter dig antingen"
" rätta formeln eller spara den som text för senare redigering. Om en formel "
"har korrekt syntax men ger en orimlig beräkning, till exempel division med "
"noll, visas ett felvärde som anger felet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:383
msgid ""
"Formulas can also contain functions which denote the use of standard "
"mathematical, business, statistical, and scientific calculations. These "
"functions take the place of any data element in a formula and can therefore "
"be combined with the standard arithmetic operators described above."
msgstr ""
"Formler kan också innehålla funktioner för vanliga matematiska, ekonomiska, "
"statistiska och naturvetenskapliga beräkningar. Funktioner kan ersätta ett "
"dataelement i en formel och kombineras med de vanliga räkneoperatorerna "
"ovan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:391
msgid ""
"These functions have the form: <_:example-1/> where FUNCTIONNAME indicates "
"the name of a function and ARGUMENTS indicates one or more arguments to the "
"function. The function arguments are separated by commas "
"(<keysym>,</keysym>)."
msgstr ""
"Funktioner skrivs på formen <_:example-1/>, där FUNCTIONNAME är funktionens "
"namn och ARGUMENTS är ett eller flera argument. Funktionsargument avgränsas "
"med kommatecken (<keysym>,</keysym>)."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:408
msgid ""
"While the documentation generally refers to functions and to cells in "
"capital letters, their use is not actually case sensitive."
msgstr ""
"Även om dokumentationen oftast skriver funktionsnamn och cellreferenser med "
"versaler gör Gnumeric ingen skillnad på stora och små bokstäver."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:415
msgid ""
"Some examples of the use of functions are: <_:example-1/> The arguments of "
"the functions vary in number from none, as in the PI() function, to an "
"unlimited number, as in the SUM() function, depending on the type of "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Här följer några exempel på funktioner: <_:example-1/> Antalet argument "
"varierar beroende på funktionen: PI() tar inga argument, medan SUM() kan ta "
"hur många som helst."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:445
msgid ""
"Formulas can include the displayed data from other cells. These contents are"
" described as `cell references' which are names indicating that the contents"
" of other cells should be used in the calculation."
msgstr ""
"Formler kan använda värden som visas i andra celler. Dessa anges med "
"cellreferenser, alltså namn som talar om att innehållet i andra celler ska "
"ingå i beräkningen."
